==Trivia==
*The shotgun is a long-barreled firearm designed to shoot a straight-walled cartridge known as a shotshell, which discharges numerous small spherical projectiles called shot. Shotguns come in a wide variety of calibers and gauges ranging from 5.5 mm to up to 5 cm. Almost all are breechloading, and can be single barreled, or in Hunter's case, double barreled. Shotguns are far less common in military use than rifles or pistols, but are a lot more common in law enforcement use.
*The Hunter is likely inspired by [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Shelly Shelly] from Brawl Stars, another Supercell game. This is referenced a few times:
**During the global release of Brawl Stars celebration, the Hunter was reskinned as Shelly in the [[Heist]] [[:Category:Modes|mode]].
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Shelly and uses the Hunter in their [[Battle Decks|deck]].
*The Hunter is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] [[cards]] to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Hunter is 1 of 4 troops that can deal damage to multiple units with one attack without an area damage radius, the others being [[Electro Spirit]], Electro Dragon, and [[Electro Wizard]].
*The Hunter's attack load shares the same sound effects as the Musketeer's deploy sound.
*If the Hunter performed his attack right before dying while being cursed by the [[Mother Witch]], it is possible for the Cursed Hog to spawn right inside these bullets, destroying it immediately.
*The Hunter is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Hunter is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
**The Hunter is the subject of a [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] item.
*The Hunter was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/h3IOFTfT8Sk?si=wTF1FekCifpSULn- Clash Royale League 2020 Tournament], by a player called Ruben.
*The initial balance change for Hunter on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2024)|6/8/2024 balance changes]] was a 4% hitpoints increase, but it was raised to 5% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-62-balance-wip last minute].
*The Hunter was originally going to have a hook mechanic, similarly to the Fisherman. However, the hook mechanic [https://www.reddit.com/r/ClashRoyale/comments/atmpr5/official_what_weve_been_up_to_this_week_feb_22/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x&context=3 were dropped], which lead to the creation of the Hunter. Ultimately, the Fisherman was added in one of Clash Royale's updates.

